href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101091"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-03T18:17:16Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2746133760,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6jrq0A","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101091#pullrequestreview-2746133760","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101091","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101091#pullrequestreview-2746133760"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101091"}},"submitted_at":"2025-09-06T18:25:56Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3193642912,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6-Wx-g","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Sorry for the delay, to be honest I'm having a hard time wrapping my head around this code. Like I can review the inner method code, and it looks mostly good aside from some minor stuff. But the control flow is really complicated to me, and I haven't really had the concentration to give it a full review.\n\nHowever I suspect the current approach is not ready for big projects. Instances are cached based on script paths, not their own path. That means for big projects were a scene could contain a lot of scripts, this implementation would not reuse the instance between scripts. This might have quite a negative effect on memory usage.\n\nI don't have a realistic project to verify this assumption, but I think we need to cache based on owner path, and cache the loaded owner for a given script separately to prevent this potential issue.\n\nAlso just some general ideas to make the control flow easier to understand:\n- replace recursion with `while` (probably very subjective, so no requirement)\n- From my understanding `owners_path_cache` is only ever populated for the current head of the resource request queue. Using a hash map is unnecessary. Converting it to a secondary queue that is only used for the head of the resource request queue, would make the loading process more clear IMO\n- Usage of `ERR_FAIL_COND` at top of functions to make clear in what state the function is expected to be called. E.g. `_cache_current_requested_resource` has an early return is the queue is empty. This makes it hard for me to tell the context in which the method can be called. Realistically it does only make sense to call this method when the queue is not empty, so this should be an explicit error. `ERR_FAIL_COND(resource_request_queue.is_empty())`.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101091#pullrequestreview-3193642912","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101091","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101091#pullrequestreview-3193642912"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101091"}},"submitted_at":"2025-09-14T11:02:48Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3244365966,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7BYRiO","user":{"login":"dekaravanhoc","id":50260825,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMjYwODI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50260825?u=646b8a3cba813e2ca0cd5e2e8a0dbfcaa8871169&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc","html_url":"https://github.com/dekaravanhoc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dekaravanhoc/events{/privacy}",